questions.stem_md:
Differentiate with respect to $x$:

(a) $y = (x^2 - 3x + 1)(x^3 + 2x - 4)$, giving the answer as a polynomial;

(b) $y = \dfrac{x^2 + 5}{2x - 1}$, for $x \ne \dfrac{1}{2}$.

Differentiate with respect to $x$ (in each part the function is defined on the interval chosen):

(a) $y = x^2\sin x + \dfrac{\cos x}{x}$, for $x > 0$;

(b) $y = \dfrac{\sec x - 1}{\sec x + 1}$, for $0 < x < \dfrac{\pi}{2}$.
